7. Bridge
Definition

A Bridge connects two LAN segments and filters traffic using MAC addresses.

LAN Segment A

     ↓

   Bridge

     ↓

LAN Segment B
Main Points
Works at Data Link Layer (Layer 2)
Uses MAC addresses
Connects LAN segments
Filters network traffic

Modern switches essentially perform multiport bridging, so standalone bridges are less common.

Interview Answer

A bridge is a Data Link Layer device that connects LAN segments and filters frames using MAC addresses.

8. Bridge vs Switch

They are similar because both work mainly at Layer 2.

Bridge	Switch
Usually fewer ports	Usually many ports
Older technology	Modern/common technology
Connects LAN segments	Connects many LAN devices
Uses MAC addresses	Uses MAC addresses
Easy Concept

Think:

Switch ≈ Multi-port Bridge

