6. Repeater
Definition

A Repeater regenerates a weak/degraded signal so it can travel farther.

Example

Imagine a signal traveling a long distance:

Strong signal → → Weak signal

                    ↓

                Repeater

                    ↓

             Regenerated signal
Main Points
Physical Layer (Layer 1)
Regenerates signals
Extends communication distance
Doesn't perform routing
Interview Answer

A repeater is a Physical Layer device that regenerates signals to extend the transmission distance.
